"value","2026-10-18","image","gameplay","The live Godot build: neon territory capture and moving enemies.","src","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/tron-exonix-claude.webp","alt","The neon TRON: EXONIX game board with a player vehicle, moving enemies, and territory boundaries.","https://www.top3d.ai/demo/exonix-build/index.html","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap browser capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[82],"Claude Code","links","Related resources",[88,89,90,91],"resourceIds","section",{"_59":82,"_26":98},{"_59":96,"_26":97},{"_59":94,"_26":95},{"_59":92,"_26":93},"MCP for Blender","/resources/mcp-for-blender/","Godot MCP · Coding-Solo","/resources/godot-mcp/","Godot Engine · Official Documentation","/resources/godot-engine/","/resources/claude-code/","Creator evidence",[102],"evidence",{"_59":103,"_26":104,"_105":106},"Read how the agent workflow was assembled","https://github.com/witnesstodark/tron-exonix/blob/master/CLAUDE.md","note","The creator’s reproducible setup record explains the AI’s implementation work, human material review, generation tools, and local launch requirements.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[111],{"_59":112,"_26":113,"_105":114},"Open the complete Godot game project","https://github.com/witnesstodark/tron-exonix","Includes the Godot project, scripts, shaders, models, textures, audio, and generation scripts. Local play requires Godot 4.7 standard; API access is only needed to regenerate assets.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[120],{"_59":121,"_26":70,"_105":122},"Play TRON: EXONIX","Creator-hosted Godot web build. Click to enter the grid, press Space to deploy, use the arrow keys to move, and Escape for the menu. A keyboard and a WebGL-capable browser are recommended.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[129],{"_59":130,"_26":131,"_105":-7},"Follow the creator’s complete workflow","https://www.top3d.ai/learn/claude-godot-mcp-3d-game","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[136,137,138,139],"Play the web build and study territory capture, trail hazards, enemy movement, and sector progression.","Follow the creator’s tutorial from prototype through materials, audio, effects, and web export.","Read CLAUDE.md to understand the agent, Godot MCP, Blender review, and asset-generation workflow.","Open game/project.godot in Godot 4.7 and press F5; study the scripts alongside the included models, textures, and audio.","AI workflow / foundation context","The creator documents Claude writing gameplay, shaders, VFX, and UI while a human steers mechanics and materials. The repository includes the actual Godot game, generated assets, and the asset-generation scripts.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Asset creation tools",false,[156,157,158,159,160,161],"assetTools","Blender","Nano Banana","PATINA","Tripo","Stable Audio","ElevenLabs","Engine","Godot 4.7 · GDScript","engine","lead",[156,157,158,159,160,161],"3d","ai-assisted",[136,137,138,139],{"_59":130,"_26":131,"_18":126},{"_59":121,"_26":70,"_18":116,"_105":122},{"_59":112,"_26":113,"_179":180,"_105":114},{"_59":103,"_26":104,"_105":106},[175,176,177,178],"claude-code","godot-engine","godot-mcp","mcp-for-blender","scope","complete-project","resource:mcp-for-blender","resource","A Blender add-on and MCP server for agent-driven modeling, materials, Python execution, and visual feedback.","/resources/",{"_20":178,"_248":92,"_146":249,"_55":250,"_247":183,"_242":241,"_26":206,"_225":251,"_218":252,"_215":253,"_212":211,"_83":254},[188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_55":22,"_61":92,"_57":248,"_87":-7},{"_55":165,"_61":183,"_57":247,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":245,"_61":246,"_57":146,"_87":151},{"_55":56,"_59":243,"_61":244,"_57":55,"_87":151},{"_55":56,"_59":240,"_61":241,"_57":242,"_87":143},{"_55":83,"_59":109,"_80":238,"_57":26,"_87":-7},{"_55":83,"_59":230,"_80":231,"_57":83,"_87":-7},{"_55":77,"_59":223,"_133":153,"_80":224,"_57":225,"_87":-7},{"_55":77,"_59":216,"_133":153,"_80":217,"_57":218,"_87":-7},{"_55":77,"_59":213,"_133":153,"_80":214,"_57":215,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":210,"_61":211,"_57":212,"_87":151},{"_55":56,"_57":207,"_59":208,"_61":209},{"_55":83,"_57":201,"_59":202,"_80":203},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[204],{"_59":205,"_26":206},"Siddharth Ahuja / ahujasid","https://github.com/ahujasid/mcp-for-blender","identity","Identity & attribution","repository and linked project site confirm an independent community integration, explicitly not affiliated with Blender Foundation. No separate project or organization logo has been confirmed; do not replace it with the official Blender logo or a personal portrait.","Source reviewed","2026-10-19","verified","Tracks",[149],"dimensions","Development stages",[219,220,221,222],"stages","Gameplay & code","Assets & animation","Engines & scenes","Testing","Topics",[156,226,227,228,229],"tags","MCP","Python","3D assets","Community project","Further reading",[232,233],{"_59":236,"_26":237},{"_59":234,"_26":235},"Opt-in content and data terms","https://github.com/ahujasid/mcp-for-blender/blob/25e1fe008fc523b1a947c6f3d28510a362a0f06e/TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS.md","Telemetry defaults and controls","https://github.com/ahujasid/mcp-for-blender/blob/25e1fe008fc523b1a947c6f3d28510a362a0f06e/README.md#L808-L842",[239],{"_59":109,"_26":206},"Why it belongs here","Useful for 3D game assets and scene prototypes with viewport feedback. Formerly blender-mcp, this community bridge can execute arbitrary Python inside Blender; use trusted tasks and saved copies. The checked documentation distinguishes default minimal usage telemetry from opt-in creative-content collection; DISABLE_TELEMETRY=true disables both. Review the opt-in data terms before enabling content capture. Validate topology, scale, UVs, collision, and exports separately.","detail","Resource type","Tool","Category","Coding agents","summary","name","agents","tool",[156,226,227,228,229],[257,258,259,260],[167],[255,256],{"_59":236,"_26":237},{"_59":234,"_26":235},"code","assets","scene","test",{"_262":263},"documents",{"_264":265,"_266":267},"en",[269,273,274,275,272,276,277,278,279,280,281,282,283,284,285,286,287,288,289,290,291,292,293,294,295,296,297,298,299,300,301,302,303,304,305,306,307,271,308,270,309,310,311,312,313,314,315,316,317,318,319,320,321,322,323,324,325,326],"zh",[268,269,270,271,272],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","community-case-research","overview","catalog","contributing","media-sources","icon-sources","content-model","skills/level-design/SKILL","skills/level-design/LICENSE","skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics","skills/level-design/references/case-studies","skills/level-design/references/combat-balance","skills/level-design/references/culture-history","skills/level-design/references/foundations","skills/level-design/references/learning","skills/level-design/references/lighting-art","skills/level-design/references/optimization-release","skills/level-design/referenc